.Dd February 11, 2026
.Dt PAX 1
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm pax
.Nd POSIX archive interchange utility
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl cdnv
.Op Fl f Ar archive
.Op Fl s Ar replstr
.Op Ar pattern ...
.Nm
.Fl r
.Op Fl cdiknuvL
.Op Fl f Ar archive
.Op Fl p Ar string
.Op Fl s Ar replstr
.Op Ar pattern ...
.Nm
.Fl w
.Op Fl dituvXL
.Op Fl f Ar archive
.Op Fl s Ar replstr
.Op Fl x Ar format
.Op Ar file ...
.Nm
.Fl r
.Fl w
.Op Fl diklntuvXL
.Op Fl p Ar string
.Op Fl s Ar replstr
.Op Ar file ...
.Ar directory
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility reads, writes, lists, and copies archive members in a POSIX style interface.
This implementation supports ustar, pax extended headers, and cpio newc.
.Pp
By default extraction behavior is path-safe and strips leading
.Sq /
semantics equivalent to
.Fl -no-absolute-paths .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl r
Read/extract mode.
.It Fl w
Write/create mode.
.It Fl f Ar archive
Archive file path. If omitted, standard input/output is used.
.It Fl x Ar format
Output format for create mode: 
.Cm pax ,
.Cm ustar , or
.Cm cpio
(newc).
.It Fl s Ar replstr
Apply deterministic substitution rules in argument order.
.It Fl L
Follow symbolic links while archiving.
.It Fl n , Fl k
Do not overwrite existing extraction targets.
.It Fl p Ar string
Preserve attributes while extracting.
Recognized letters are
.Cm m
(mode),
.Cm e/t
(timestamps), and
.Cm o
(owner/group).
.It Fl v
Verbose operation.
.It Fl -no-absolute-paths
Reject unsafe archive paths and avoid extracting absolute paths.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std pax
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cpio 1 ,
.Xr tar 1
.Sh STANDARDS
The interface follows the POSIX
.Nm
model with pax extended header support for long or overflowing metadata.
